{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For</b> — then it will become clear to them that HaShem, although He is exalted above all, sees the lowly like me, who was at first a shepherd of sheep. And the meaning of 'sees' is that He will deliver me." "And the word יידע — like הכבד, such as ייטיב, and the dalet is opened [without dagesh] because of a guttural letter." "<b>From afar</b> — from a distant place, like the height of the heavens above the earth." "And the word יידע — let Him teach us knowledge, that He may chastise us, as in: ויודע בהם את אנשי סוכות (and he chastised them with the men of Succoth)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 138, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:02.900215970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}